% ============================================================================
% elements.query.adj — a worked recall over the grade-school elements library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what is oxygen's atomic
% number?": it states no chemistry fact — it only `import`s the grounded table
% and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the
% `atomic_number` rows and returns the number + the table's source/locator/trust.
% The third query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the number, recall the
% element). An element not in the table abstains honestly — the engine never
% invents an atomic number.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli elements.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "elements.adj"

? atomic_number(hydrogen, $Z)          % expect 1
? atomic_number(oxygen, $Z)            % expect 8
? atomic_number($E, 6)                 % expect carbon — the reverse recall
? atomic_number(kryptonite, $Z)        % expect abstain — not a chemical element
